      "item_id": "075b80e31faba3a92a3d7712",
      "version_id": "6d392f0b897d89aba5f23830f5b954824cd8a50f3e5b222e12b93c42db9bf552",
      "decision": "accept",
      "reason": "Published October 8, within the September 16–October 15 UTC window. Accept as an operational evaluation tutorial for students, not evidence of model superiority or autonomous research gains. The saved passage under 'The fix' specifies representative tasks, explicit evaluation criteria, fresh chats and equal file/tool access; 'Do this now' supplies a judge prompt requiring specific evidence and unverifiable claims to be flagged. These are usable procedures, although the supplied evidence does not include the linked model outputs, repeated trials, held-out tasks or measured costs. The author's statement 'ChatGPT was clearly better for my scoped research' is a personal assessment, not a general result; using ChatGPT to judge its own comparison adds potential evaluator bias. Novelty is a recent worked practitioner demonstration, not a new evaluation method. 'Dig deeper' explicitly promotes paid access to Fun Bench results, establishing a subscription interest; those gated results cannot substantiate performance here. Evidence: [saved text, 'The fix', 'Do this now', 'Dig deeper' and footnote 6](data/assets/075b80e31faba3a92a3d7712/6d392f0b897d89aba5f23830f5b954824cd8a50f3e5b222e12b93c42db9bf552/text.txt).",
      "piece_ids": ["02", "03"]
    },
    {
      "item_id": "084a91218ed6d51df5ab9f17",
      "version_id": "2b0d8382c674620fd174f5c60697d5bdf4728371aa386ebba1986c60e1eef65b",
      "decision": "accept",
      "reason": "Published September 30, within the authoritative window. Useful original researcher account of reward design and human-gated experimental automation. 'A better PLM recipe' reports contact precision rising from 28.2% to 36.6% P@L at 48.4B tokens; this is an author-reported relative improvement of about 30%, not 30 percentage points or evidence of fully autonomous discovery. 'Failure mode' reports two 72-round searches improving validation loss without matching the best contact precision, directly motivating scrutiny of proxy rewards. 'What survived the human gate' describes two seeds, a noise-aware retention rule and four of seven changes surviving scaled-up ablation. These concrete campaign details provide the new evidence and practical lessons for student experiment design. Limitations: the supplied blog lacks numerical ablation tables, hardware, total search cost, execution logs and independent replication; equal token budgets alone do not establish equal compute cost, and contact precision remains a proxy. The authors describe their own project and promote its adoption; no financial conflict is disclosed in the supplied text. Its referenced paper is the same underlying work, not independent corroboration, and workshop status is not validation. Evidence: [saved text, named sections and 'Authors and links'](data/assets/084a91218ed6d51df5ab9f17/2b0d8382c674620fd174f5c60697d5bdf4728371aa386ebba1986c60e1eef65b/text.txt).",
      "piece_ids": ["01", "02", "03"]
    },
    {
      "item_id": "090f19610270f1b804a5bb8a",
      "version_id": "bc44cd416a3cec196c5ff3ae89d1d7f5f529cfcb851b97b519470fc6baccac09",
      "decision": "accept",
      "reason": "Published September 30, within the authoritative window. Accept primarily for methodological scrutiny and student lessons about preserving hypotheses, executable states and verification records. Sections 3.2–3.4 specify the idea pool, compatible-parent restoration and evaluator; section 4 supplies baselines, an M4 Pro/24 GB setup, one-hour or twelve-hour horizons, and token accounting. The new contribution is the coupled search organization and its reported benchmark evaluation, not training agent weights. Treat the preprint's performance claims as provisional: section 4.2 calls 1,070,460 tokens a total, while section 4's Metrics defines token values as averages across instances. Table 4 places AutoMIP's sole 6–12-hour success at 41,089 seconds, whereas Appendix H records that late success, acopf_caseactivsg70k_qcqp, at 24,199 seconds. These discrepancies require reconciliation before publishing cost or timing headlines. 'New best' solution claims also lack objective values and independently checked solution certificates in the supplied per-instance tables. Several protocol appendices contain only headings; Appendix B identifies its prompts as standardized templates rather than historical prompts. No independent replication or external researcher assessment is supplied. This is the developers' own evaluation; financial interests are not disclosed here. Evidence: [saved text, §§3–4, Table 4 and Appendices A, B and H](data/assets/090f19610270f1b804a5bb8a/bc44cd416a3cec196c5ff3ae89d1d7f5f529cfcb851b97b519470fc6baccac09/text.txt).",
      "piece_ids": ["02", "03"]
    },
    {
      "item_id": "0ff8643be07c7b70497b5caf",
      "version_id": "b5c10a5a1f3bc0adb95fe7a8ee96127189a24131d2304c6d0f00b108ccee3a5f",
      "decision": "accept",
      "reason": "Published October 7, within the authoritative window. Strong fit for all three pieces: the new evidence combines agent-written kernel components, trusted assembly, frozen validation selection, held-out families and matched search ablations. Appendix A.6 reports failures among numerically screened unrestricted programs of 12/35, 18/31 and 8/37; these support scrutiny of finite tests, not a universal failure rate. Preserve the qualification in Proposition 1 and Appendix A.1: kernel validity assumes finite, correctly shaped, pure components; sampled conformance tests do not prove purity throughout the domain. Appendices B.5–B.7 distinguish ablation campaigns from headline campaigns and show important limits: broader frozen DWF prediction wins only 44/88 synthetic comparisons and 4/16 real-data comparisons. Appendix D.3 attributes much forecasting advantage to reversed windows and reports stronger CAKE results at the ten-year forward horizon. Appendix E.2 uses simulated patients, and none of its 35 nMSE contrasts survives the stated Holm correction. These findings constrain broad superiority claims rather than being averaged away. For students, the inference is to separate proposal, verification and selection and test beyond the discovery distribution. Appendix D.1 provides calls, tokens and timing, but not a complete hardware/dollar budget. This is an author-run preprint without supplied independent replication; author affiliations and financial conflicts remain unresolved. Some code/prompt listings are absent from the supplied extraction, limiting reproducibility claims. Evidence: [saved text, Proposition 1 and Appendices A.1, A.6, B.5–B.7, D.1, D.3 and E.2](data/assets/0ff8643be07c7b70497b5caf/b5c10a5a1f3bc0adb95fe7a8ee96127189a24131d2304c6d0f00b108ccee3a5f/text.txt).",
      "piece_ids": ["01", "02", "03"]
    }
  ]
}
